engine marzano(0.1)
language ruby

// @dialect ruby
// Ruby sources (`.rb`) are parsed by the pinned upstream `tree-sitter-ruby`
// grammar (ABI 14) that the frozen Grit closure already carries. Grit returns
// syntax matches plus logged source values; Attune assigns repository
// identities, resolves and admits edges, and derives inverse relations one
// layer above this frontend.

// @syntax source
//
// Literal relative requires.
//
// Both written forms match. Ruby parses a parenthesized call as a `call` node
// and a bare command as a `command_call` node, so the frontend names both:
//
//   require_relative "pricing"
//
//   require_relative("pricing")
//
// The match is the whole require and the logged value is the argument list:
//
//   "pricing"
//
//   ("pricing")
//
// The exact text between the match start and the logged arguments is the
// requiring method, so `require_relative` is recoverable the same way a
// declaration keyword is. Attune's Flix resolver takes the logged argument
// text, keeps it only when it is one single quoted literal (with any wrapping
// parentheses removed), resolves it against the requiring file's directory, and
// admits the target only when exactly one admitted file matches.
//
// Everything else stays explicitly unresolved instead of being guessed here:
//
//   require_relative File.join("shop", "pricing")   -> computed require
//
//   require_relative "absent_pricing"               -> missing file
//
//   require "json"                                  -> not a relative require
//
// The first two still match, so Attune's Flix admission sees the non-literal or
// absent target and reports the import as explicitly unresolved rather than
// inventing an edge. Absolute and gem requires name no repository file and are
// deliberately excluded by the logged method name.
//
// @example A literal relative require is a static file dependency.
// require_relative "pricing"
// @end

or {
  call(arguments = $arguments),
  command_call(arguments = $arguments)
} as $import where {
  $import <: contains identifier() as $method,
  $method <: r"^require_relative$",
  log(message="import", variable=$arguments)
}
